/**
 * @mainpage MIDILAR
 *
 * MIDILAR is the MIDI layer of the RoModular ecosystem: MIDI 1.0 and MIDI 2.0
 * protocol, messages, parsing, routing and real-time devices for desktop and
 * embedded targets, built on Foundation (general utilities), DspCore (signal
 * processing) and MCC (music
 * theory). Devices use Universal MIDI Packets internally. Native MIDI 1.0
 * message builders also expose complete bytes directly, with explicit UMP
 * conversion when needed.
 *
 * @note Latest release: 0.3.3. Native MIDI 1.0 builders and the recovered
 * protocol topics are working-tree additions documented under Unreleased.
 * Stock Arduino C++11 source builds are supported.
 *
 * @section MIDILARMainModules Modules
 *
 * - @ref MIDILAR_Core "Core": MIDILAR, MCC and Foundation version information.
 * - @ref MIDILAR_Protocol "Protocol": channels, groups, values, UMP packets,
 *   MIDI 1.0 and USB MIDI 1.0 translation, MIDI Time Code and MCC pitch
 *   conversions.
 * - @ref MIDI_Protocol "MIDI 1.0 protocol guide": message layouts, controller
 *   and channel-mode topics, real-time, system common, MTC and SysEx.
 * - @ref MIDILAR_Midi1 "Native MIDI 1.0 messages": the adapted Message API,
 *   memory model and migration from the historical implementation.
 * - @ref MIDILAR_Devices "Devices": filters, transforms, scale filter and
 *   chord generation, router, MIDI clock, step sequencer and MTC.
 *
 * Hardware transports are separate libraries built on the Protocol
 * conversions. The rules MIDILAR types follow are collected in the
 * @ref MIDILAR_Specification "MIDI-Domain Specification".
 *
 * @section MIDILARMainDependency Dependencies
 *
 * MIDILAR links `Foundation::Foundation` (Foundation 2.0 or a newer 2.x
 * release, built on CPSTL) and `MCC::MCC` (MCC 0.6.0 or a newer 0.x release). It uses local
 * packages when available and otherwise fetches the pinned releases from
 * GitHub; see @ref MIDILAR_BuildGuide_Dependency.
 */
